The invention is a pharmaceutical packaging apparatus that includes:

- a **drug supply unit** configured to supply one or more drugs;
- a **packaging unit** that packages the supplied drugs using packaging paper;
- a **paper conveying unit** that conveys the packaging paper along a conveyance path through a printing area; and
- an **ink ejection unit** that ejects ink onto the packaging paper in the printing area to print information such as patient data, drug details, or administration instructions.

The conveying path includes an **upstream conveyance-direction switching section** located upstream of the printing area and a **downstream conveyance-direction switching section** located downstream of the printing area. These switching sections selectively change the direction or route in which the packaging paper is conveyed, allowing the paper to pass through, reverse through, or be repositioned relative to the printing area. This arrangement enables flexible printing on selected portions or surfaces of the packaging paper while maintaining coordinated drug supply and packaging operations.

### Object

The object is to provide a drug-packaging device capable of printing prescription information—such as the patient’s name, drug name, dosage, and administration time—directly on packaging paper without placing a platen, backing plate, or other support beneath the printing area. This simplifies the paper path, avoids friction and contamination, and facilitates paper replacement and maintenance.

### Configuration

The drug-packaging device **(1)** principally includes:

- a drug-supply section **(2)** for dispensing prescribed drugs;
- a packaging-paper supply section **(3)** holding a roll of packaging paper **(4)**;
- guide rollers **(5)** and a tensioning member **(6)** that convey and tension the paper;
- a non-contact printing unit **(7)** having an inkjet print head **(8)**;
- a drug-charging section **(9)** that introduces the dispensed drugs onto or between portions of the paper;
- a sealing unit **(10)**, typically including heat-sealing rollers **(11)**; and
- a cutting or perforating unit **(12)** for separating successive drug packets.

At the printing position, the packaging paper **(4)** extends as a tensioned, unsupported span between upstream and downstream guide members **(5)**. The inkjet print head **(8)** is positioned close to one surface of this span and ejects ink without contacting the paper. No platen or supporting base is located opposite the print head.

A controller **(13)** coordinates paper movement, drug dispensing, and the operation of the print head **(8)** so that the required information is printed at the position corresponding to each drug packet. After printing, the drugs are inserted, and the packaging paper is sealed and divided into individual packets.

The key feature is therefore the combination of a **non-contact print head (8)** with a **tension-controlled, unsupported printing span of packaging paper (4)**.
